  "comments": [
    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "can someone explain the difference between this and just [node] ?",
      "html": "can someone explain the difference between this and just [node] ?",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "e66c2ab143936216239068aa121b6e07d8ccfa44fe2333b8d9b7b93ca10b767f",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "I think it is simply that if the clause before node is a noun, such as in this example, then you use 'nanode'. If it is a verb then you only use 'node'. \n\nAs far as I know, 'na' seems to be related to the copula 'da', and can be seen in other similar circumstances such as 'nanoni'. Exactly why it changes to na instead of da I don't know. \n\nContrast 'sou da to omou',and 'sou na node...'",
      "html": "I think it is simply that if the clause before node is a noun, such as in this example, then you use 'nanode'. If it is a verb then you only use 'node'. <br/><br/>As far as I know, 'na' seems to be related to the copula 'da', and can be seen in other similar circumstances such as 'nanoni'. Exactly why it changes to na instead of da I don't know. <br/><br/>Contrast 'sou da to omou',and 'sou na node...'",
      "credits_raw": "bi-ru",
      "content_sha256": "07ec9f5c0b0f5cbd17fbfeced4afbb0690af006ac1e8735ccc472a738faf156a",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "な is 連体形 of 助動詞「だ」which inflect as だろ、で、だっ、だ、な、なら but な only connects to particles の、ので、のに.",
      "html": "な is 連体形 of 助動詞「だ」which inflect as だろ、で、だっ、だ、な、なら but な only connects to particles の、ので、のに.",
      "credits_raw": "bamboo4",
      "content_sha256": "ae1b28f4bb01d5b1a98548e2662ca18c1e3e16707301be21600dc74ba66bd129",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    }
